NNAAMMEE
     col - remove reverse and half line motions

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ccooll [-bbddffxx] [-pp_n]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ccooll reads the standard input and writes the standard output.
     It removes reverse and half-line motions (as produced by
     nnrrooffff) by keeping an image of the page in memory and perfor-
     ming those motions against that image, so that only forward
     motion appears on the output.

     ccooll recognizes the following characters and escape sequences
     in its input: newline, carriage return, backspace, and tab
     carry their usual meaning; the escape character (033)
     followed by 77, 88, 99, or BB is taken as a full reverse line
     feed, half reverse line feed, half forward line feed, or
     full forward line feed, respectively; the control character
     VVTT (013) is an alternate form of full reverse line feed; the
     control characters SSOO (017) and SSII (016) mark the start and
     end of an alternate character set, which ccooll remembers per
     character and reproduces with matching SSOO / SSII pairs on out-
     put.  An escape character followed by any other character is
     discarded along with that character.  All other control
     characters are discarded.

     When two or more characters are destined for the same output
     position (an overstrike), ccooll remembers all of them and,
     unless -bb is given, writes them as a backspace-separated
     overstrike sequence.  Runs of spaces on output are entabbed
     to every eighth column unless -xx is given.

     -bb   The output device cannot backspace.  Only the last
          character destined for a given position is written;
          earlier overstruck characters are discarded.

     -dd   Double-space the output: where the input has no inter-
          vening half line, print two newlines instead of one.
          Overridden by -ff.

     -ff   The output device can handle forward half-line motions,
          so ccooll writes half lines as physical half-line motions
          instead of folding them onto full lines.  Takes
          precedence over -dd.

     -pp_n  Set the size of the internal page buffer to _n lines
          (default 128).  Lines outside the buffered window are
          written out as the window advances.

     -xx   Do not convert runs of spaces on output into tabs.

